Package: tidyABM
Title: Agent-Based Modelling with Tidy Data and a Declarative Grammar
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Rayhan Ali", "Rachman", email = "rayhanalirachman@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A declarative grammar for writing agent-based models (ABMs) in R.
    Models are described as data rather than as loops: a setup block declares the
    agent population, an optional network and shared globals, and a behavioural
    block declares an ordered sequence of typed steps (matching, rules, births,
    deaths and global updates). Agents are stored as tibbles and rules are written
    as 'dplyr'-style formulas, so a model reads as a specification and its output
    is tidy data ready for analysis. The design follows the block structure of
    'NetLogo' (setup / go) while keeping the interface idiomatic to the tidyverse.
